Hi, Like many I have been dissatisfied with the GPS performance. Based on some info in this post I have replaced the "Jumpstar JS-H210" module that came with the radio with an "ATGM336H-5N31" module. I did not change the antenna or any other components in the radio. <br><br>I'm now getting a cold start GPS position in about 45 seconds outdoors, which is a big improvement.<br><br>The module is a direct replacement.<br><br>Here is the Aliexpress link to the chip. <br><a href="https://vi.aliexpress.com/item/1005006980194824.html?spm=a2g0o.order_list.order_list_main.5.3be91802yOLKqV&amp;gatewayAdapt=glo2vnm" class="postlink">https://vi.aliexpress.com/item/10050069 ... pt=glo2vnm</a><br><br>I masked of the surrounding components with Kapton tape and used a hot air station to remove the chip old chip. Then some solder wick and alcohol to clean up the pads. Then soldered the new chip on. <br><br>Mike VK4MWL<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=837">VK4MWL</a> — Sat Feb 15, 2025 11:12 pm</p><hr />
